From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:39:54 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 029/230] Order the onboarding anchor after the follow and
 repair its victims
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The first pick fired the follow POST and the anchor PUT concurrently, so
the anchor 404'd NOT_FOLLOWING before the follow row existed — silently,
since the mutation had no onError. New users ended up with zero anchors,
breaking the schema's "exactly one anchor" rule (12 users at audit time).

- src/lib/favoriteAnchor.ts owns the ordering: the anchor never fires
  before the follow settles, transient anchor failures (network/5xx/429)
  retry once, terminal 4xxs do not, and failures propagate.
- useFavorites gains toggleAndAnchor (cap checks unchanged); Onboarding's
  first-pick branch uses it instead of the racing pair.
- setAnchor now surfaces errors through the shared toast instead of
  vanishing.
- tests/anchorRace.test.ts pins the ordering, the never-on-follow-failure
  rule, the bounded retry and the retry classification.
- server/dev/repairAnchors.ts (npm run repair:anchors) fixes existing
  zero-anchor users by anchoring their earliest follow; dry-run by
  default, --apply writes and then re-verifies. Run against a DB copy:
  12 repairable → 0 left, idempotent on re-run.

